  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPrincipal (P) = ₹10,000\n\nAmount (A) = ₹12,100\n\nTime (t) = 2 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nA = P(1 + r/100)t\n\nWhere, r = annual interest rate\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n12,100 = 10,000(1 + r/100)²\n\n⇒ (1 + r/100)² = 12,100 ÷ 10,000\n\n⇒ (1 + r/100)² = 1.21\n\n⇒ (1 + r/100) = √1.21\n\n⇒ (1 + r/100) = 1.1\n\n⇒ r/100 = 1.1 - 1\n\n⇒ r/100 = 0.1\n\n⇒ r = 0.1 × 100\n\n⇒ r = 10%\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**\n\n34:T",
